1
00:00:02,001 --> 00:00:03,378
Hey, guys.

2
00:00:03,420 --> 00:00:05,172
( all greeting )

3
00:00:05,213 --> 00:00:07,174
We need to talk to you
about something.

4
00:00:07,215 --> 00:00:08,467
Yeah, we don't feel

5
00:00:08,509 --> 00:00:10,302
like we can host Thanksgiving
this year.

6
00:00:10,344 --> 00:00:12,638
What?!
Are you kidding?

7
00:00:12,680 --> 00:00:15,307
Well, it's just with, uh, work
and the stress of adoption,

8
00:00:15,349 --> 00:00:17,100
we don't feel like
we have the energy.

9
00:00:17,142 --> 00:00:18,435
Plus, we don't think
it's fair

10
00:00:18,477 --> 00:00:20,270
that every year
the burden falls on us.

11
00:00:20,312 --> 00:00:24,441
That doesn't sound like you.

12
00:00:24,483 --> 00:00:27,402
That's Monica talking!

13
00:00:27,444 --> 00:00:29,279
No, no.

14
00:00:29,321 --> 00:00:31,949
We made
this decision together.

15
00:00:31,991 --> 00:00:34,284
She's putting words
in your mouth!

16
00:00:34,326 --> 00:00:36,286
Don't you put words
in people's mouths.

17
00:00:36,328 --> 00:00:38,121
You put turkey in
people's mouths.

18
00:00:39,748 --> 00:00:40,875
I can't believe this.

19
00:00:40,916 --> 00:00:42,751
This is Emma's
first Thanksgiving.

20
00:00:42,793 --> 00:00:43,961
No, it's not.

21
00:00:44,003 --> 00:00:45,044
It's not?

22
00:00:45,086 --> 00:00:47,130
When was she born?

23
00:00:49,132 --> 00:00:50,467
Well, personally,
I think it's great

24
00:00:50,509 --> 00:00:51,802
you're giving yourself a break.

25
00:00:51,844 --> 00:00:52,970
Thank you, Pheebs.

26
00:00:53,012 --> 00:00:54,638
Sure. It's just as well.

27
00:00:54,680 --> 00:00:56,724
I mean, last year
wasn't very good.

28
00:00:56,765 --> 00:00:58,642
I think she's
losing her touch.

29
00:00:58,684 --> 00:01:00,811
What?!
You are way off, lady!

30
00:01:00,853 --> 00:01:02,021
Am I? Really?

31
00:01:02,062 --> 00:01:03,522
Am I?

32
00:01:03,564 --> 00:01:05,649
Well, why don't you cook
Thanksgiving dinner

33
00:01:05,691 --> 00:01:06,692
and prove me wrong?

34
00:01:08,402 --> 00:01:09,737
Well, think about it.

35
00:01:09,778 --> 00:01:12,322
You'd be trying to top
what you did last year.

36
00:01:12,364 --> 00:01:14,825
You'd be in a competition
with yourself.

37
00:01:14,867 --> 00:01:17,995
That's my favorite kind.

38
00:01:18,037 --> 00:01:19,663
Okay, we are
doing this!

39
00:01:19,705 --> 00:01:22,791
Don't let yourself
get manipulated this way.

40
00:01:22,833 --> 00:01:24,710
Stay out of
this, Chandler!

41
00:01:24,752 --> 00:01:27,086
This is between me and me!

42
00:01:28,714 --> 00:01:32,175
We are supposed to make
these decisions together.

43
00:01:32,217 --> 00:01:35,345
Did you not watch the Dr. Phil
I taped for you?

44
00:01:42,394 --> 00:01:47,274
♪ So no one told you
life was gonna be this way ♪

45
00:01:47,315 --> 00:01:49,484
♪ Your job's a joke,
you're broke ♪

46
00:01:49,526 --> 00:01:51,946
♪ Your love life's D.O.A. ♪

47
00:01:51,987 --> 00:01:57,200
♪ It's like you're always
stuck in second gear ♪

48
00:01:57,242 --> 00:01:59,369
♪ When it hasn't been
your day, your week ♪

49
00:01:59,411 --> 00:02:01,663
♪ Your month,
or even your year ♪

50
00:02:01,705 --> 00:02:05,542
♪ But I'll be there for you ♪

51
00:02:05,584 --> 00:02:08,045
♪ When the rain starts to pour ♪

52
00:02:08,087 --> 00:02:10,589
♪ I'll be there for you ♪

53
00:02:10,631 --> 00:02:13,300
♪ Like I've been there before ♪

54
00:02:13,341 --> 00:02:16,053
♪ I'll be there for you ♪

55
00:02:16,095 --> 00:02:19,890
♪ 'Cause you're there
for me, too. ♪

56
00:02:28,774 --> 00:02:30,818
Hey.
Hi.

57
00:02:30,859 --> 00:02:32,235
Happy Thanksgiving!

58
00:02:32,277 --> 00:02:34,655
Oh, yeah, happy
Needless Turkey Murder Day.

59
00:02:36,281 --> 00:02:37,866
Hey, guys, I ordered
some chocolate pies

60
00:02:37,908 --> 00:02:39,034
from that bakery on Bleeker.

61
00:02:39,076 --> 00:02:40,368
Could you pick them up for me?

62
00:02:40,410 --> 00:02:42,203
You're not making
the pies yourself?

63
00:02:42,245 --> 00:02:43,580
No, I don't make chocolate pies.

64
00:02:43,622 --> 00:02:44,790
When I was younger,

65
00:02:44,832 --> 00:02:46,166
I entered
this pie eating contest

66
00:02:46,207 --> 00:02:47,584
and I ate so many

67
00:02:47,626 --> 00:02:49,461
that just the thought of them
makes me sick.

68
00:02:49,503 --> 00:02:51,338
Did you at least
win the contest?

69
00:02:51,379 --> 00:02:54,591
Two minutes, 12 pies,
and a part of one tin.

70
00:02:56,093 --> 00:02:57,636
Okay, I'll see you guys at 4:00.

71
00:02:57,678 --> 00:02:58,887
Can't wait.

72
00:02:58,929 --> 00:03:00,472
This dinner is going
to be so great.

73
00:03:00,514 --> 00:03:02,683
In your face, Last Year Me!

74
00:03:04,852 --> 00:03:07,186
Hey, Rach, what's
Emma doing today?

75
00:03:07,228 --> 00:03:09,064
Well, let's see,
uh, I know

76
00:03:09,106 --> 00:03:12,400
that she has a meeting
with her lawyer,

77
00:03:12,442 --> 00:03:16,030
and then she has to make
a very big poop.

78
00:03:16,071 --> 00:03:17,698
Why?

79
00:03:17,739 --> 00:03:20,450
Well, I want to enter her
in a baby beauty pageant.

80
00:03:20,492 --> 00:03:21,910
Oh, my God.

81
00:03:21,952 --> 00:03:24,245
That's the creepiest thing
I've ever heard.

82
00:03:24,287 --> 00:03:25,580
Okay, but

83
00:03:25,622 --> 00:03:27,332
before you say no,
my friend Suzanne

84
00:03:27,374 --> 00:03:29,543
is entering her kid
and compared to Emma,

85
00:03:29,584 --> 00:03:30,752
she's a real dog.

86
00:03:30,794 --> 00:03:33,881
Oh! Phoebe,
all babies are beautiful.

87
00:03:33,922 --> 00:03:36,383
Uh, okay.

88
00:03:36,424 --> 00:03:37,718
Just the idea

89
00:03:37,759 --> 00:03:39,469
of pitting one baby
against another,

90
00:03:39,511 --> 00:03:41,513
I mean, you know,
judging who's cuter

91
00:03:41,555 --> 00:03:42,681
just for a trophy...

92
00:03:42,723 --> 00:03:43,932
And $1,000.

93
00:03:43,974 --> 00:03:46,768
...is something
I'm very interested in.

94
00:03:48,103 --> 00:03:50,480
Oh, please,
do not tell Ross.

95
00:03:50,522 --> 00:03:52,024
He still believes

96
00:03:52,066 --> 00:03:54,193
that what's on the inside
is important.

97
00:03:54,233 --> 00:03:56,361
Okay. Ooh, Emma needs
a cowgirl outfit

98
00:03:56,403 --> 00:03:57,696
for the competition.

99
00:03:57,738 --> 00:03:59,364
Where am I going to get
a cowgirl outfit

100
00:03:59,406 --> 00:04:00,448
on Thanksgiving?

101
00:04:00,490 --> 00:04:01,992
Well, I was thinking...

102
00:04:02,034 --> 00:04:03,785
Take the clothes
off Joey's Cabbage Patch Kid!

103
00:04:03,827 --> 00:04:05,537
Yeah.

104
00:04:09,624 --> 00:04:11,292
( marching band playing )

105
00:04:11,334 --> 00:04:13,712
( laughing )

106
00:04:13,754 --> 00:04:16,006
Did someone drop
the baton again?

107
00:04:16,048 --> 00:04:19,676
Why come all the way from Kansas
to do that?

108
00:04:22,303 --> 00:04:25,640
I don't get older,
I just get better.

109
00:04:25,682 --> 00:04:27,601
You know
what just occurred to me?

110
00:04:27,642 --> 00:04:29,644
This could be
our last Thanksgiving

111
00:04:29,686 --> 00:04:30,896
just the two of us.

112
00:04:30,938 --> 00:04:33,107
I mean,
we could be getting a baby soon.

113
00:04:33,148 --> 00:04:34,108
You don't know that.

114
00:04:34,149 --> 00:04:35,734
Somebody's going to pick us.

115
00:04:35,776 --> 00:04:37,360
Yeah, but we haven't heard
a thing

116
00:04:37,402 --> 00:04:39,654
from the adoption agency,
and it's been weeks.

117
00:04:39,696 --> 00:04:41,156
I'm telling you,
it's going to happen.

118
00:04:41,198 --> 00:04:42,616
Next year, it's going
to be you, me

119
00:04:42,657 --> 00:04:45,202
and little Hemingway Bing.

120
00:04:46,703 --> 00:04:48,622
What? He's my favorite author.

121
00:04:48,663 --> 00:04:49,873
Name one of his books.

122
00:04:55,712 --> 00:04:57,338
The Firm?

123
00:04:57,380 --> 00:04:59,007
Okay, let's see.

124
00:04:59,049 --> 00:05:02,844
Okay, the turkey's in the oven;
the stuffing is ready...

125
00:05:02,886 --> 00:05:05,472
You know, you always cook
this meal all by yourself.

126
00:05:05,513 --> 00:05:07,099
Let me help this year.

127
00:05:07,141 --> 00:05:08,433
Aw, Chandler,
that's sweet.

128
00:05:08,475 --> 00:05:10,185
But you don't have
to do everything

129
00:05:10,227 --> 00:05:11,519
Dr. Phil tells you to do.

130
00:05:11,561 --> 00:05:12,687
I'm serious.

131
00:05:12,729 --> 00:05:14,022
Let me do something.

132
00:05:14,064 --> 00:05:16,357
Just not the turkey
or the stuffing.

133
00:05:16,399 --> 00:05:17,859
Nothing high-profile.

134
00:05:17,901 --> 00:05:18,944
Okay, let's see.

135
00:05:18,986 --> 00:05:20,612
Oh, the cranberry sauce.

136
00:05:20,654 --> 00:05:21,738
It's easy to make,

137
00:05:21,780 --> 00:05:23,782
and no one
really cares about it.

138
00:05:23,824 --> 00:05:26,076
Tell me more.

139
00:05:26,118 --> 00:05:29,204
Okay, I'm going to go check
on something across the hall.

140
00:05:29,246 --> 00:05:30,664
You start
by washing these.

141
00:05:32,916 --> 00:05:34,001
Not with soap!

142
00:05:38,088 --> 00:05:42,676
You obviously haven't tasted
my Palmolive potatoes.

143
00:05:43,718 --> 00:05:45,804
Hey, hey, guess what Joey has?

144
00:05:45,846 --> 00:05:47,848
Three tickets
to today's Rangers game!

145
00:05:47,889 --> 00:05:49,474
Dude, I wanted him to guess.

146
00:05:49,516 --> 00:05:50,767
Oh.

147
00:05:50,809 --> 00:05:51,935
Oh, my God!

148
00:05:51,977 --> 00:05:53,520
Yeah, they're
great seats, too.

149
00:05:53,561 --> 00:05:55,147
Guess where they are.

150
00:05:55,189 --> 00:05:56,564
Center ice.

151
00:05:56,606 --> 00:05:59,651
Did I do something to you?

152
00:06:01,820 --> 00:06:02,904
Mmm, the game's at 1:00.

153
00:06:02,946 --> 00:06:04,405
ROSS:
So?

154
00:06:04,447 --> 00:06:05,866
Dinner's at 4:00.
We'll never make it back.

155
00:06:05,907 --> 00:06:07,075
We'll leave
before it's over.

156
00:06:07,117 --> 00:06:08,076
We'll be back in time.

157
00:06:08,118 --> 00:06:09,703
You say that now,

158
00:06:09,744 --> 00:06:11,705
but it could take us
a long time to get back home.

159
00:06:11,746 --> 00:06:13,207
Plus, Joey could get lost

160
00:06:13,248 --> 00:06:15,876
and they could have to page us
to go pick him up.

161
00:06:15,917 --> 00:06:18,419
Dude, two times
that happened!

162
00:06:19,378 --> 00:06:22,090
Look, Monica's been working hard
all day.

163
00:06:22,132 --> 00:06:24,134
She didn't want to host
this thing in the first place.

164
00:06:24,176 --> 00:06:25,468
We shouldn't go.

165
00:06:25,510 --> 00:06:26,511
He's right, man.

166
00:06:26,553 --> 00:06:27,679
Yeah, I guess.

167
00:06:27,721 --> 00:06:29,056
All right,
so we'll see you at 4:00.

168
00:06:29,097 --> 00:06:30,598
Okay.

169
00:06:30,640 --> 00:06:34,353
And get ready to taste
my very special cranberries.

170
00:06:34,393 --> 00:06:36,980
Or should I say... Chanberries.

171
00:06:40,483 --> 00:06:43,528
That's some gentle comedy,
dude.

172
00:06:43,570 --> 00:06:45,947
We're still going
to the game, right?

173
00:06:45,989 --> 00:06:47,490
Yeah.
Yeah.

174
00:06:51,494 --> 00:06:52,495
Our next contestant

175
00:06:52,537 --> 00:06:54,081
is a two-year-old.

176
00:06:54,122 --> 00:06:56,208
Her name is Jacqueline,
and she comes from Mount Kisco.

177
00:06:56,250 --> 00:06:57,458
Oh, Phoebe, listen,

178
00:06:57,500 --> 00:06:58,793
I think we got to go.

179
00:06:58,835 --> 00:07:00,170
This place is really
freaking me out.

180
00:07:00,212 --> 00:07:01,504
I've been watching
this guy over there.

181
00:07:01,546 --> 00:07:03,924
I don't think he
came with a kid.

182
00:07:03,965 --> 00:07:05,508
But we can't leave now.

183
00:07:05,550 --> 00:07:08,303
There was this one baby, Hayley,
who was favored to win,

184
00:07:08,345 --> 00:07:10,638
and she got croup,
so she had to stay home.

185
00:07:10,680 --> 00:07:13,058
This competition
just blew wide open, folks.

186
00:07:13,100 --> 00:07:15,643
Phoebe, it's just too weird.

187
00:07:15,685 --> 00:07:17,020
I just saw a one-year-old

188
00:07:17,062 --> 00:07:18,855
running around
with pantyhose on.

189
00:07:18,897 --> 00:07:21,400
I know. We should
have been more prepared.

190
00:07:22,109 --> 00:07:23,443
It's okay.

191
00:07:23,484 --> 00:07:24,778
Now, the way I see it,

192
00:07:24,819 --> 00:07:26,821
our real competition now
is Cameron.

193
00:07:26,863 --> 00:07:27,948
Oh, my God.

194
00:07:27,989 --> 00:07:29,408
They just took
her sweater off.

195
00:07:29,448 --> 00:07:30,450
Look at those arms.

196
00:07:30,491 --> 00:07:31,492
Hello, Michelin man.

197
00:07:31,534 --> 00:07:32,786
Oh, Phoebe!

198
00:07:32,827 --> 00:07:34,037
Come on!

199
00:07:34,079 --> 00:07:35,496
You know, it's
already 3:00.

200
00:07:35,538 --> 00:07:37,416
They haven't even gotten
to Emma's group.

201
00:07:37,457 --> 00:07:38,792
We got to go. We got dinner.

202
00:07:38,833 --> 00:07:40,460
But Emma's got what it takes!

203
00:07:40,501 --> 00:07:41,962
She could go all the way!

204
00:07:43,713 --> 00:07:46,049
Phoebe, you have to calm down.

205
00:07:46,091 --> 00:07:51,054
Okay, Rachel, the hottest
babies in the tri-state area

206
00:07:51,096 --> 00:07:53,681
are in this room right now.

207
00:07:55,558 --> 00:07:57,185
I overheard
one of the judges say

208
00:07:57,227 --> 00:07:59,438
that not one of them
holds a candle to Emma.

209
00:07:59,479 --> 00:08:01,022
Really?
Yeah.

210
00:08:01,064 --> 00:08:02,523
You heard him say that?

211
00:08:02,565 --> 00:08:03,817
Yeah.

212
00:08:03,858 --> 00:08:05,193
All right. Okay.

213
00:08:05,235 --> 00:08:07,195
All right,
let's give these babies

214
00:08:07,237 --> 00:08:08,571
something to cry about.

215
00:08:08,613 --> 00:08:10,740
Good! Okay!
Let's get down to business.

216
00:08:10,782 --> 00:08:12,075
Emma needs some makeup.

217
00:08:12,117 --> 00:08:13,534
What?!

218
00:08:13,576 --> 00:08:14,702
She's going to look
all washed out

219
00:08:14,744 --> 00:08:16,246
next to the other contestants.

220
00:08:16,288 --> 00:08:18,539
Phoebe, I am not letting you
put makeup on my baby.

221
00:08:18,581 --> 00:08:20,917
Why not?
Because I already did!

222
00:08:26,756 --> 00:08:29,676
Oh! You bum!
Oh, you suck!

223
00:08:29,717 --> 00:08:32,762
Get off the ice!
You idiot!

224
00:08:32,804 --> 00:08:33,805
What a game!

225
00:08:33,847 --> 00:08:35,849
I know!

226
00:08:35,890 --> 00:08:38,226
I can't believe Chandler
is missing this.

227
00:08:38,268 --> 00:08:41,188
Yeah, I'm sorry
he's not here too,
but I got to say,

228
00:08:41,229 --> 00:08:43,064
I am really enjoying
Nacho Chair.

229
00:08:43,106 --> 00:08:45,066
Yeah, I'd probably
enjoy it more

230
00:08:45,108 --> 00:08:47,610
if you didn't keep
batting my hand away.

231
00:08:47,652 --> 00:08:49,363
( yelling )
Oh, yeah!

232
00:08:49,404 --> 00:08:51,031
These seats are great!

233
00:08:51,072 --> 00:08:52,324
I know, I know.

234
00:08:52,366 --> 00:08:54,201
When I was here
for Holidays on Ice...

235
00:08:55,785 --> 00:08:57,745
I was sitting so far away,

236
00:08:57,787 --> 00:09:00,707
Michelle Kwan
couldn't read my banner.

237
00:09:00,748 --> 00:09:01,833
Whoa, hey, we better get going.

238
00:09:01,875 --> 00:09:03,043
If we don't leave right now,

239
00:09:03,084 --> 00:09:04,085
we're going
to be late for dinner.

240
00:09:04,127 --> 00:09:05,379
Oh, but it's a tie game.

241
00:09:05,420 --> 00:09:07,088
So, we're a little late,
you know?

242
00:09:07,130 --> 00:09:08,382
The girls will be there.

243
00:09:08,423 --> 00:09:10,133
Let's just stay
for one more goal.

244
00:09:10,175 --> 00:09:11,092
I don't know.

245
00:09:11,134 --> 00:09:12,802
One more fight.
Okay.

246
00:09:17,265 --> 00:09:18,308
Where is everybody?

247
00:09:18,350 --> 00:09:19,726
They're 45 minutes late.

248
00:09:19,767 --> 00:09:21,602
I can't believe
they're not here.

249
00:09:21,644 --> 00:09:24,814
I slaved and I slaved for what?

250
00:09:24,856 --> 00:09:27,359
They've ruined Cranberry Day!

251
00:09:28,735 --> 00:09:30,945
How late are we?

252
00:09:30,987 --> 00:09:32,030
45 minutes.

253
00:09:32,072 --> 00:09:33,323
Wow.
Here.

254
00:09:33,365 --> 00:09:34,782
Okay.

255
00:09:34,824 --> 00:09:36,368
Rachel and Phoebe
are already there, okay?

256
00:09:36,410 --> 00:09:38,078
So, they probably started
without us.

257
00:09:38,119 --> 00:09:39,287
We can just slip in,

258
00:09:39,329 --> 00:09:40,914
and no one needs to know
where we were.

259
00:09:41,998 --> 00:09:45,252
You may want to lose
the foam finger.

260
00:09:45,293 --> 00:09:46,627
Oh, no, no, no, no, no.

261
00:09:46,669 --> 00:09:48,838
You just want to put it
on your hand.

262
00:09:50,298 --> 00:09:51,758
Hey.
( gasping )

263
00:09:51,799 --> 00:09:52,926
Oh!

264
00:09:52,967 --> 00:09:54,928
You're not at
Thanksgiving?

265
00:09:54,969 --> 00:09:56,179
No!

266
00:09:56,221 --> 00:09:57,264
No, we're late!

267
00:09:57,305 --> 00:09:58,306
What are you
doing here?!

268
00:09:58,348 --> 00:09:59,433
We're late, too!

269
00:09:59,474 --> 00:10:01,142
( gasping and squealing )

270
00:10:01,184 --> 00:10:02,269
We figured
we could be late

271
00:10:02,310 --> 00:10:03,520
because you guys
would be on time.

272
00:10:03,562 --> 00:10:05,272
Don't point that thing
at me, Tribbiani.

273
00:10:06,731 --> 00:10:07,815
So, nobody's here?!

274
00:10:07,857 --> 00:10:09,067
Monica's going
to kill us.

275
00:10:09,109 --> 00:10:10,277
Yeah, where were you?

276
00:10:10,318 --> 00:10:11,778
ROSS:
Yeah, what's
with the trophy?

277
00:10:11,819 --> 00:10:12,987
Um, well, uh...

278
00:10:13,029 --> 00:10:15,490
We were at
a spelling bee.

279
00:10:17,658 --> 00:10:19,369
And I won!

280
00:10:19,411 --> 00:10:24,124
You won an adult
Thanksgiving Day
spelling bee?

281
00:10:24,165 --> 00:10:27,168
Yes. Y-E-S-- yes.

282
00:10:27,210 --> 00:10:29,796
Let me see this.

283
00:10:29,837 --> 00:10:33,508
"Grand Supreme Little Darling,
New York Division"?

284
00:10:33,550 --> 00:10:36,136
That's me.

285
00:10:36,177 --> 00:10:39,389
You entered Emma
in a beauty pageant?!

286
00:10:39,431 --> 00:10:44,936
And it looks like
she put makeup on her.

287
00:10:44,978 --> 00:10:46,605
Wait a second,
wait a second.

288
00:10:46,646 --> 00:10:49,274
Where have I seen that
cowgirl outfit before?

289
00:10:49,316 --> 00:10:51,151
I can't believe this.

290
00:10:51,192 --> 00:10:52,860
She's our daughter.

291
00:10:52,902 --> 00:10:55,530
That you would treat her
like some kind of show dog

292
00:10:55,572 --> 00:10:56,697
is inexcusable!

293
00:10:56,739 --> 00:10:58,241
She won $1,000!

294
00:10:58,283 --> 00:11:00,910
So, this is
an annual thing?

295
00:11:02,912 --> 00:11:04,164
( gasping )

296
00:11:04,205 --> 00:11:06,166
That's Alicia May
Emory's outfit!

297
00:11:08,751 --> 00:11:10,378
You guys,
there are people in there

298
00:11:10,420 --> 00:11:11,963
who are not getting
any happier.

299
00:11:12,005 --> 00:11:13,256
Yeah, what
are we going to do?

300
00:11:13,298 --> 00:11:14,549
I don't know.
You guys figure it out.

301
00:11:14,591 --> 00:11:15,758
I got to put Emma down
for her nap.

302
00:11:15,800 --> 00:11:16,968
And Rach, while
you're in there,

303
00:11:17,010 --> 00:11:18,178
throw something
on Alicia May!

304
00:11:19,929 --> 00:11:22,223
All right,
what are we going to say?

305
00:11:22,265 --> 00:11:24,058
Ooh! We'll say
that we were mugged.

306
00:11:24,100 --> 00:11:27,562
You can't get mad
at someone who's been mugged.

307
00:11:27,604 --> 00:11:28,813
Good, that's good.

308
00:11:28,855 --> 00:11:29,939
But you don't look
like you were mugged.

309
00:11:29,981 --> 00:11:31,983
No. Here.

310
00:11:35,694 --> 00:11:37,531
Hey!

311
00:11:38,865 --> 00:11:41,284
Do you hear something?

312
00:11:45,955 --> 00:11:47,040
They're out there!

313
00:11:47,081 --> 00:11:48,082
( gasping )

314
00:11:48,124 --> 00:11:49,125
Let me see!

315
00:11:50,669 --> 00:11:52,337
Oh, my God,
I can't believe this.

316
00:11:52,379 --> 00:11:53,672
They're an hour late,

317
00:11:53,712 --> 00:11:56,715
and they're just standing
out there talking!

318
00:11:56,757 --> 00:11:58,759
Everything's so distorted.

319
00:11:58,801 --> 00:12:01,555
It looks like Joey
has a giant hand.

320
00:12:03,348 --> 00:12:04,599
That says Rangers on it.

321
00:12:04,641 --> 00:12:06,059
They went to the game!
( gasping )

322
00:12:06,100 --> 00:12:09,896
Oh, they are in
for a world of pain.

323
00:12:11,856 --> 00:12:13,483
Ross' shirt is torn.

324
00:12:13,525 --> 00:12:15,985
They're late,
and they're sloppy!

325
00:12:17,736 --> 00:12:19,072
All right,
Emma's napping.

326
00:12:19,113 --> 00:12:20,532
What happened
to your shirt?

327
00:12:20,574 --> 00:12:24,578
I got mugged,
and they stole my pocket.

328
00:12:25,744 --> 00:12:28,873
We're trying
to figure out
an excuse.

329
00:12:28,915 --> 00:12:31,000
Hey, oh, how
about this?

330
00:12:31,042 --> 00:12:33,503
We could say that
Monica told us
5:00, not 4:00.

331
00:12:33,545 --> 00:12:35,088
That way, we're
right on time.

332
00:12:35,129 --> 00:12:36,381
Or...!

333
00:12:38,049 --> 00:12:40,677
we could plant PCP
in the apartment

334
00:12:40,719 --> 00:12:42,136
and call the cops on her.

335
00:12:43,555 --> 00:12:45,181
That would be a good way

336
00:12:45,223 --> 00:12:48,351
to get rid of all the PCP
we have lying around.

337
00:12:48,393 --> 00:12:50,228
We'll just say
that she said it was 5:00.

338
00:12:50,270 --> 00:12:51,271
We'll just act casual.

339
00:12:51,312 --> 00:12:52,355
We're not late.

340
00:12:52,397 --> 00:12:53,398
We're right on time.

341
00:12:59,279 --> 00:13:00,863
"We know you're out there."

342
00:13:00,905 --> 00:13:02,490
( gasping )

343
00:13:04,909 --> 00:13:07,078
( sotto voce ):
Who do you think
it's from?

344
00:13:15,794 --> 00:13:17,422
Oh, God, this is bad.

345
00:13:17,464 --> 00:13:18,881
This is so bad.

346
00:13:18,923 --> 00:13:20,883
Well, let's just go in there
and face them.

347
00:13:20,925 --> 00:13:22,135
Well, I'm not
going in first.

348
00:13:22,176 --> 00:13:23,802
I bet that vein
on Monica's forehead

349
00:13:23,844 --> 00:13:26,180
is popping like crazy.

350
00:13:26,222 --> 00:13:27,557
Yeah, I hate that thing.

351
00:13:27,599 --> 00:13:30,226
It's like a bolt
of lightning.

352
00:13:30,268 --> 00:13:31,478
Oh, hey, I have an idea.

353
00:13:31,519 --> 00:13:33,062
Why don't we play
Rock, Paper, Scissors,

354
00:13:33,104 --> 00:13:34,397
and whoever loses
goes in first.

355
00:13:34,439 --> 00:13:35,398
Okay.
All right,
I'm in.

356
00:13:35,440 --> 00:13:36,441
Ready?

357
00:13:41,112 --> 00:13:43,364
Ha, ha! I win!

358
00:13:43,406 --> 00:13:44,574
What is that?

359
00:13:44,616 --> 00:13:47,410
That's fire.
Beats everything.

360
00:13:47,452 --> 00:13:49,203
Oh, really? Does it beat
water balloon?

361
00:13:49,245 --> 00:13:50,664
( puncturing noise
and hissing )
Oh...

362
00:13:52,582 --> 00:13:56,586
Well played, Phoebe
Buffay, well played.

363
00:13:56,628 --> 00:13:57,754
All right, enough, come on.

364
00:13:57,796 --> 00:13:58,879
Let's just go in
at the same time.

365
00:13:58,921 --> 00:14:00,089
ALL:
Okay, okay.

366
00:14:02,592 --> 00:14:03,760
It's locked.

367
00:14:03,802 --> 00:14:05,303
Wha...? Oh, sure,

368
00:14:05,345 --> 00:14:07,555
now they lock it,
but when they're having sex

369
00:14:07,597 --> 00:14:09,182
on the couch, it's like,

370
00:14:09,223 --> 00:14:12,185
"Come on in.
My butt is surprisingly hairy."

371
00:14:13,770 --> 00:14:15,062
All right, come on.

372
00:14:15,104 --> 00:14:16,397
All right, you guys!

373
00:14:16,439 --> 00:14:17,982
We're so sorry
we're late!

374
00:14:18,024 --> 00:14:20,610
Please let us in so we
can have dinner together.

375
00:14:20,652 --> 00:14:21,611
No!

376
00:14:21,653 --> 00:14:22,612
Everything's cold.

377
00:14:22,654 --> 00:14:23,904
The turkey's dried out,

378
00:14:23,946 --> 00:14:25,573
and the-the
stuffing's all soggy!

379
00:14:25,615 --> 00:14:28,242
Yeah, and there's a bowl
of cranberry sauce that's...

380
00:14:28,284 --> 00:14:30,244
What happens
to cranberry sauce?

381
00:14:30,286 --> 00:14:31,579
Nothing. It's fine.

382
00:14:31,621 --> 00:14:33,790
Oh, thank God!

383
00:14:33,832 --> 00:14:35,583
Come on, you guys.
We're sorry.

384
00:14:35,625 --> 00:14:38,085
Our-our subway broke down.

385
00:14:38,127 --> 00:14:39,295
That's a lie!
You went to the game.

386
00:14:39,337 --> 00:14:41,381
I can see Joey's hand.

387
00:14:41,422 --> 00:14:43,675
For the love of
God, take it off!

388
00:14:46,469 --> 00:14:47,554
You guys, come on.

389
00:14:47,595 --> 00:14:48,638
It doesn't matter

390
00:14:48,680 --> 00:14:49,806
why we're late.

391
00:14:49,848 --> 00:14:51,516
We're all here now.

392
00:14:51,558 --> 00:14:53,184
Please let us in so we can have
some of your delicious turkey.

393
00:14:54,477 --> 00:14:56,103
( laughs )

394
00:14:56,145 --> 00:14:59,315
I had a dream once about
a fax machine that did that.

395
00:15:01,192 --> 00:15:02,901
That's all the turkey
you're going to get!

396
00:15:02,943 --> 00:15:04,696
How are we going to
decide who gets this?

397
00:15:04,738 --> 00:15:05,905
Water balloon!

398
00:15:11,411 --> 00:15:12,704
What are we going to do?

399
00:15:12,746 --> 00:15:14,247
I'm starving.

400
00:15:14,288 --> 00:15:15,665
( gasps ):
Oh, I just remembered!

401
00:15:15,707 --> 00:15:17,208
We do have
something to eat.

402
00:15:17,250 --> 00:15:19,419
Monica put something in
our oven this morning.

403
00:15:19,460 --> 00:15:21,920
Hey, you touch that,
and you will be sorry.

404
00:15:21,962 --> 00:15:23,381
Guys, I'd listen to her.

405
00:15:23,423 --> 00:15:25,592
The vein is bigger
than I've ever seen it!

406
00:15:28,928 --> 00:15:30,054
Voila.
( laughs )

407
00:15:30,096 --> 00:15:32,515
Oh, my God,
it's Brussels sprouts!

408
00:15:32,557 --> 00:15:35,101
That's worse than no food!

409
00:15:35,142 --> 00:15:39,856
Ha, ha! All you got
was Monica's stinky
Brussels sprouts!

410
00:15:39,898 --> 00:15:41,357
Stinky?

411
00:15:41,399 --> 00:15:44,736
Please let me stay on
this side of the door.

412
00:15:44,778 --> 00:15:47,363
Oh, I know!
I still have my old key.

413
00:15:47,405 --> 00:15:48,531
Ooh.

414
00:15:48,573 --> 00:15:50,825
We can just unlock the door.

415
00:15:50,867 --> 00:15:52,577
Well, I don't know if
that's such a good idea.

416
00:15:52,619 --> 00:15:54,662
They clearly don't
want to be with us.
You know what?

417
00:15:54,704 --> 00:15:56,873
I don't want to be
with them either,
but it's Thanksgiving,

418
00:15:56,915 --> 00:15:58,666
and we should not want to be
together together!

419
00:15:59,709 --> 00:16:00,877
If I could just get in there

420
00:16:00,919 --> 00:16:02,629
and make a face-to-face apology,

421
00:16:02,670 --> 00:16:03,963
you know,
look 'em in the eye,

422
00:16:04,004 --> 00:16:05,548
I know can I get 'em
to forgive us.

423
00:16:05,590 --> 00:16:07,926
I don't know...
I'm telling you...

424
00:16:10,929 --> 00:16:12,931
I can do it.

425
00:16:13,932 --> 00:16:15,600
Yeah, he can do it.

426
00:16:17,811 --> 00:16:19,395
RACHEL:
Oh.

427
00:16:19,437 --> 00:16:20,939
JOEY:
All right.

428
00:16:23,483 --> 00:16:25,401
Oh...

429
00:16:25,443 --> 00:16:27,570
It all looks so beautiful.

430
00:16:27,612 --> 00:16:29,739
The turkey, the stuffing...

431
00:16:29,781 --> 00:16:31,741
The cranberries.
( scoffs )

432
00:16:31,783 --> 00:16:34,452
Enough! A monkey
could've made 'em!

433
00:16:39,666 --> 00:16:43,586
Hey, listen, guys,
we feel really terrible.

434
00:16:43,628 --> 00:16:46,840
He's doing that weird
eye-contact thing.

435
00:16:46,881 --> 00:16:49,592
Don't look at him.
Don't look at him.

436
00:16:49,634 --> 00:16:51,177
Come on, you guys.

437
00:16:51,218 --> 00:16:54,388
We want you to know
we're very, very sorry.

438
00:16:55,431 --> 00:16:56,891
Right, guys?

439
00:16:58,058 --> 00:17:00,979
ROSS:
I feel terrible.
So sorry.

440
00:17:02,647 --> 00:17:03,857
But let's not ruin this day.

441
00:17:03,898 --> 00:17:05,274
You've worked so hard.

442
00:17:05,316 --> 00:17:06,818
Let's move past this,

443
00:17:06,860 --> 00:17:08,778
and try to have a nice meal
all together, huh?

444
00:17:08,820 --> 00:17:10,989
The floating heads
do make a good point.

445
00:17:13,324 --> 00:17:14,909
Yeah, they do seem
to feel pretty bad.

446
00:17:14,951 --> 00:17:15,910
So bad.
So bad.

447
00:17:15,952 --> 00:17:17,662
So bad.

448
00:17:18,663 --> 00:17:20,707
Okay.

449
00:17:20,748 --> 00:17:23,710
Okay, you two go get
the dessert,

450
00:17:23,751 --> 00:17:25,837
and I'll let you in.

451
00:17:25,879 --> 00:17:28,715
Dessert?

452
00:17:28,756 --> 00:17:31,551
Yeah, I asked you and Phoebe
to pick up the pies.

453
00:17:31,592 --> 00:17:33,469
You did remember, right?

454
00:17:33,511 --> 00:17:36,764
Pies. Oh, we thought
you said "prize."

455
00:17:38,182 --> 00:17:40,267
Here.

456
00:17:43,437 --> 00:17:45,857
Grand Supreme Little Darling?

457
00:17:45,899 --> 00:17:48,192
Congratulations!

458
00:17:49,694 --> 00:17:51,988
Oh, my God,
you forgot the pies?!

459
00:17:52,030 --> 00:17:53,489
Well, I can't believe this!

460
00:17:53,531 --> 00:17:54,991
You forced me to make dinner,

461
00:17:55,033 --> 00:17:56,325
then you're an hour late,

462
00:17:56,367 --> 00:17:57,994
and you forget
the one little thing

463
00:17:58,036 --> 00:17:59,370
that I asked you to do!

464
00:17:59,412 --> 00:18:01,539
Really, girls, not cool.

465
00:18:03,541 --> 00:18:06,168
Well, you man-heads
aren't any better.

466
00:18:06,210 --> 00:18:07,879
You lied about going
to the game.

467
00:18:07,921 --> 00:18:10,590
You knew it would make you late,
and you still went anyway.

468
00:18:10,631 --> 00:18:12,216
Hey! I'm getting a little tired
of this, okay.

469
00:18:12,258 --> 00:18:13,634
We said we're sorry!

470
00:18:13,676 --> 00:18:15,177
It's Thanksgiving,
for Pete's sakes!

471
00:18:15,219 --> 00:18:16,679
A day of forgiveness!

472
00:18:16,721 --> 00:18:18,014
It's a day to be thankful.

473
00:18:18,056 --> 00:18:19,557
Don't make me come up there.

474
00:18:21,059 --> 00:18:23,603
Fine.
It's too late for apologies.

475
00:18:23,644 --> 00:18:25,772
Let's just go.
I don't need your stupid dinner.

476
00:18:25,813 --> 00:18:28,858
That would be a lot
more convincing if
you weren't drooling.

477
00:18:28,900 --> 00:18:30,860
Ew! Is that what that is?

478
00:18:30,902 --> 00:18:32,570
Sorry.

479
00:18:32,612 --> 00:18:33,988
Come on, you guys.

480
00:18:34,030 --> 00:18:36,699
Let's just do
our own Thanksgiving.

481
00:18:36,741 --> 00:18:37,700
Yeah, I'll cook.

482
00:18:37,742 --> 00:18:39,201
Yeah, let's go out.

483
00:18:39,243 --> 00:18:40,578
Hey!

484
00:18:41,996 --> 00:18:44,373
Yeah, you three
have a nice Thanksgiving.

485
00:18:44,415 --> 00:18:45,750
Yeah.
The three of us?

486
00:18:45,792 --> 00:18:47,919
You, Chan, and the vein!

487
00:18:47,961 --> 00:18:49,003
( gasps )

488
00:18:50,880 --> 00:18:52,130
( scoffs )

489
00:18:55,551 --> 00:18:57,845
( gags )

490
00:18:57,887 --> 00:19:00,723
Uh-oh. I'm stuck.

491
00:19:00,765 --> 00:19:02,558
Joey, that is not going to work.
No, seriously.

492
00:19:04,226 --> 00:19:05,937
I'm really wedged in here.

493
00:19:05,979 --> 00:19:08,064
I'll pull you through.
Okay.

494
00:19:08,106 --> 00:19:09,315
Ow, ow, ow, ow! Stop, stop!

495
00:19:09,356 --> 00:19:11,275
I'm worried
about damaging my head.

496
00:19:11,317 --> 00:19:12,944
It's a little late for that.

497
00:19:14,403 --> 00:19:16,155
Well, hurry up.
You got to do something.

498
00:19:16,196 --> 00:19:17,197
All right, well,

499
00:19:17,239 --> 00:19:18,699
this does not change
anything.

500
00:19:18,741 --> 00:19:19,993
Okay, we need
to get something

501
00:19:20,034 --> 00:19:21,368
to grease the sides
of his face.

502
00:19:21,410 --> 00:19:22,453
Uh, we got turkey grease.

503
00:19:22,495 --> 00:19:23,621
Bring it.

504
00:19:23,663 --> 00:19:25,039
I just want to say
that I'm sorry

505
00:19:25,081 --> 00:19:27,875
I referred to the vein
as a separate person.

506
00:19:27,917 --> 00:19:29,209
All right, here you go.

507
00:19:29,251 --> 00:19:30,294
Okay.

508
00:19:30,336 --> 00:19:32,755
Ooh, that smells good.

509
00:19:34,590 --> 00:19:35,925
Mm-hmm.

510
00:19:41,097 --> 00:19:43,933
Okay.
Okay, try it.

511
00:19:45,768 --> 00:19:47,937
It isn't working!

512
00:19:47,979 --> 00:19:49,772
All right, we're going
to have to unscrew the chain.

513
00:19:49,814 --> 00:19:51,607
Well, hurry.
I can't feel my ears.

514
00:19:51,649 --> 00:19:53,317
Can you ever feel your ears?

515
00:19:54,360 --> 00:19:56,612
Interesting.

516
00:19:56,654 --> 00:19:58,489
Chandler, where are
your tools?

517
00:19:58,531 --> 00:20:01,075
Ooh, I left them
on my bulldozer.

518
00:20:03,828 --> 00:20:06,413
I don't have tools.

519
00:20:06,455 --> 00:20:08,833
Well, I do,
but Rachel borrowed them.

520
00:20:08,875 --> 00:20:10,084
I lent them to Ross.

521
00:20:10,126 --> 00:20:11,418
I gave them to Joey.

522
00:20:11,460 --> 00:20:13,629
I left them at the park.

523
00:20:15,548 --> 00:20:18,134
I'm finding it really hard
not to mess with him.

524
00:20:18,176 --> 00:20:20,636
I've already stuffed
a bunch of Brussels
sprouts down his pants.

525
00:20:20,678 --> 00:20:21,637
Nice.

526
00:20:21,679 --> 00:20:22,930
( phone ringing )

527
00:20:22,972 --> 00:20:24,598
Okay... I have to get that.

528
00:20:24,640 --> 00:20:25,850
Now, when I get back,

529
00:20:25,892 --> 00:20:28,102
I want you and your friends
to be gone.

530
00:20:28,144 --> 00:20:29,937
Thanksgiving is over!

531
00:20:29,979 --> 00:20:32,690
The vein has spoken!

532
00:20:33,733 --> 00:20:35,275
It's really starting to hurt.

533
00:20:35,317 --> 00:20:38,029
Okay, look, I'm... I'm
going to pull on the door,

534
00:20:38,071 --> 00:20:39,697
and you guys push
as hard as you can.

535
00:20:39,739 --> 00:20:42,366
Maybe we can get enough room
to wiggle him out, okay?

536
00:20:42,408 --> 00:20:43,534
Okay, so push!

537
00:20:43,576 --> 00:20:45,078
PHOEBE:
Just a sec.

538
00:20:45,119 --> 00:20:47,663
We're kind of in the
middle of something here.

539
00:20:47,705 --> 00:20:50,541
Oh! Stop putting things
down my pants!

540
00:20:50,583 --> 00:20:51,876
Come on, guys, push!

541
00:20:51,918 --> 00:20:53,044
Yeah, come on!

542
00:20:53,086 --> 00:20:56,214
Push! Push! Push!
Push! Push! Push!

543
00:20:56,254 --> 00:20:58,340
( grunts )
( screams )

544
00:20:58,382 --> 00:21:00,259
RACHEL:
Oh!

545
00:21:05,223 --> 00:21:07,725
My cranberries!

546
00:21:07,767 --> 00:21:10,603
Oh, man, I got food all over me!

547
00:21:13,064 --> 00:21:14,648
Ah! I can't believe
what you did!

548
00:21:14,690 --> 00:21:16,025
Monica's going to kill you!

549
00:21:16,067 --> 00:21:18,318
Look, look, look what the...
look what...

550
00:21:18,360 --> 00:21:20,863
look, look, look what
floating heads did!

551
00:21:22,364 --> 00:21:24,408
I don't care.

552
00:21:25,701 --> 00:21:27,620
What's going on?

553
00:21:28,662 --> 00:21:30,957
That was the adoption agency.

554
00:21:30,998 --> 00:21:32,792
And...?

555
00:21:32,833 --> 00:21:35,836
We're getting a baby!

556
00:21:35,878 --> 00:21:37,880
Are you serious?!

557
00:21:42,927 --> 00:21:46,764
There's a pregnant woman
in Ohio, and she picked us.

558
00:21:46,806 --> 00:21:48,808
( all cheering )

559
00:21:50,810 --> 00:21:53,312
I'm so happy for you.

560
00:21:55,231 --> 00:21:59,110
This Thanksgiving kicks
last Thanksgiving's ass!

561
00:21:59,152 --> 00:22:00,987
Whoo!

562
00:22:05,992 --> 00:22:08,327
To Monica and
Chandler...

563
00:22:08,368 --> 00:22:11,080
and that knocked-up girl
in Ohio.

564
00:22:11,122 --> 00:22:12,832
Hear, hear.

565
00:22:15,501 --> 00:22:18,671
I'm just so happy you guys
are finally getting a kid.

566
00:22:18,712 --> 00:22:20,256
PHOEBE:
I know.

567
00:22:20,298 --> 00:22:22,300
Have you considered
pageanting?

568
00:22:24,426 --> 00:22:26,553
I can't believe they called.

569
00:22:26,595 --> 00:22:29,890
We're actually getting a baby.

570
00:22:29,932 --> 00:22:31,934
Oh, I know how you feel.

571
00:22:33,019 --> 00:22:34,687
Really?

572
00:22:34,728 --> 00:22:37,148
Sure. I went through
the exact same thing

573
00:22:37,190 --> 00:22:38,774
with Alicia May Emory.

574
00:22:41,527 --> 00:22:43,821
The waiting, the wondering...

575
00:22:43,863 --> 00:22:47,533
then one day, I get that call
from Toys "R" Us.

576
00:22:48,534 --> 00:22:51,578
She was in stock.

577
00:22:51,620 --> 00:22:53,956
That is the exact same thing.

578
00:22:53,998 --> 00:22:56,876
